    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good way to put it. but honestly, some people say that \"social capital\" is just a fancy way to justify keeping things the way they were and preventing actual progress or diversity. it feels like the argument for \"stability\" is almost always used to silence people who want change. do you think there's a point where clinging to these traditions actually becomes a net negative for a modern country?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
